@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@
+# Solyanka GUI/HUD Premium Audit
+
+## Scope and method
+
+This is a source-level audit of every registered feature card, settings panel, HUD entry, dedicated screen, and shared rendering primitive in the current checkout. The benchmark is `Move Hotbar`, especially `HotbarPainter` and `HotbarPrimitives`.
+
+The audit is intentionally conservative: it distinguishes existing behavior from design recommendations and does not claim in-game visual QA on a Linux build machine.
+
+## Benchmark: what Move Hotbar already gets right
+
+`Move Hotbar` is the visual source of truth because it has:
+
+- Four explicit visual presets: Vanilla, Minimal, Glass, and Neon.
+- A reusable surface model: background, secondary color, accent, opacity, radius, border width, gradient, shadow, glow, shimmer, selection opacity, and effect radius.
+- Real rounded geometry rather than square fill rectangles.
+- Layered depth: shadow first, surface second, border third, sheen/glow last.
+- Bounded gradients clipped to rounded corners.
+- Motion tied to elapsed time rather than arbitrary frame counters.
+- A clear separation between content geometry and visual appearance.
+- Conservative alpha and glow values that preserve readability.
+- A layout model that calculates bounds before drawing, preventing overlap and off-screen placement.
+
+Every other surface should use the same contract:
+
+```kotlin
+data class SurfaceStyle(
+    val preset: Preset,
+    val background: Color,
+    val secondary: Color,
+    val accent: Color,
+    val opacity: Float,
+    val radius: Float,
+    val borderWidth: Float,
+    val shadow: Boolean,
+    val glow: Boolean,
+    val shimmer: Boolean,
+    val effectSpeed: Float,
+)
+```
+
+## Global design tokens
+
+Use the existing dark Solyanka palette, but make it semantic and consistent:
+
+| Token | Value | Use |
+|---|---:|---|
+| Canvas | `#0B111B` | GUI background / HUD void |
+| Surface | `#16202E` | Base card |
+| Raised | `#263448` | Button, selected card, header |
+| Border | `#435870` | Default boundaries |
+| Text | `#EDF4FD` | Primary text |
+| Muted | `#B2C2D8` | Descriptions and secondary metadata |
+| Accent | `#7DD3FC` | Focus, selection, links |
+| Positive | `#80E0B0` | Enabled / connected |
+| Warning | `#F3ACAC` | Disabled / caution |
+| Error | `#FF5555` | Validation and failures |
+
+Spacing scale: `3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24`. Default radius: `5–7`. Default border: `1`. Never use color as the only state indicator: pair it with text, a border, or a shape change.
+
+## Total screen audit
+
+### 1. `NoFrillsClickGui` — main feature browser
+
+**Current weaknesses**
+
+- Feature cards are visually consistent but mostly static.
+- Search and category columns do not have a strong hierarchy between navigation, content, and active state.
+- Footer hints are plain text placed against the world with no dedicated surface.
+- Focus/hover feedback is primarily a border color change.
+- The horizontal multi-column layout becomes dense when many categories are visible.
+
+**Required upgrade**
+
+- Add a fixed top chrome band with brand, active category, search state, and close action.
+- Give each category a compact header with an accent rail and count badge.
+- Animate card hover/selection with a 2–4 px lift and accent interpolation over 160–220 ms.
+- Add a selected-card glow only for the active feature; keep idle cards quiet.
+- Put keyboard/mouse hints inside a bottom status capsule, not directly on the world.
+- Use a compact two-column layout at narrow widths rather than forcing horizontal scrolling.
+
+**Presets**
+
+- Minimal: opaque navy cards, one blue accent line, no glow.
+- Glass: translucent cards, white top sheen, low-opacity border.
+- Neon: stronger accent halo, animated shimmer only on selected cards.
+- Amber: orange accent for dungeon-focused sessions.
+
+### 2. `SettingsPanel` and `GuiKit`
+
+**Current weaknesses**
+
+- Shared controls are structurally good but rows are mechanically uniform.
+- Long panels lack enough grouping and hierarchy.
+- Toggles, sliders, colors, and descriptions do not communicate semantic importance consistently.
+- Error/status text is a single footer label and can be missed.
+
+**Required upgrade**
+
+- Use `GuiKit.section` for every long panel, not just Yandex Music.
+- Add an accent rail and section subtitle.
+- Make errors a raised red status card with an icon/text prefix.
+- Keep labels at one size and descriptions at one muted size.
+- Add a consistent hover surface to buttons and color controls.
+- Preserve the current instant-save model; visual feedback should not imply a separate Save action.
+
+### 3. `HudEditorScreen`
+
+**Current weaknesses**
+
+- Preview rectangles are flat and do not communicate live-vs-sample state strongly enough.
+- The canvas has no alignment grid, safe-area guides, or snap feedback.
+- Selection and hover are both border-only.
+- The top controls and bottom status text float over the world without a surface.
+
+**Required upgrade**
+
+- Add a low-alpha 8 px grid and 16 px major grid.
+- Add safe-area guides at 8 px and 16 px from the screen edge.
+- Render selected HUDs with the same premium surface painter used by Move Hotbar.
+- Add a small selected-state chip with name, position, scale, and enabled state.
+- Animate selection changes and drag preview; commit the final position at release.
+- Add keyboard nudges in 1 px and Shift+arrow in 8 px increments.
+
+### 4. `Move Hotbar` — benchmark
+
+**Status:** strongest implementation in the project.
+
+**Preserve:** four presets, rounded clipping, glow/shadow, shimmer, selection animation, explicit layout model.
+
+**Small refinements:** centralize its surface math into a reusable theme primitive so other HUDs cannot drift visually.
+
+## HUD-by-HUD audit
+
+### Vanilla HUD / Move Hearts
+
+Current native replacement/follower behavior is functional but inherits vanilla visual density.
+
+- Add a shared glass/neon surface behind moved followers only when the selected style is not Vanilla.
+- Keep native icons and bars untouched in Vanilla mode.
+- Add low-alpha separators between health, armor, and XP followers.
+- Use consistent rounded corners and accent colors from the selected theme.
+
+### Timers: Goldor, Storm Pad, Storm Lightning, Storm PY, Storm Phase, M3 Fire Freeze
+
+Current timer entries are text-oriented and can look like isolated labels.
+
+- Convert each timer to a compact status capsule with left accent rail.
+- Use semantic urgency colors: blue idle, amber imminent, red active/late, green complete.
+- Animate only the progress/urgent state, never the text itself.
+- Keep a stable width to prevent HUD jitter as numbers change.
+- Theme options: Minimal capsule, Glass capsule, Neon countdown ring.
+
+### Player Display: health, mana, overflow, defense, vitality, EHP, speed
+
+Current feature has many independent HUDs, which makes a unified visual language important.
+
+- Provide a shared stat-card painter with icon slot, label, value, and optional progress rail.
+- Keep value alignment fixed so changing digits do not move neighboring text.
+- Group related stats with the same accent family.
+- Use small icon badges instead of extra words when the icon is unambiguous.
+- Theme options: compact text, glass stat tiles, neon rails.
+
+### Picture in Picture
+
+Current explicit-window capture is a strong functional boundary but needs presentation chrome.
+
+- Add a title bar with capture state and source label.
+- Add rounded clipping, subtle border, and connection indicator.
+- Show a non-intrusive empty state when no capture is selected.
+- Never add fake blur or pretend the source is live when it is stale.
+- Theme options: clean frame, glass frame, neon recording frame.
+
+### Pet Display
+
+Current sample-oriented display can read as a plain information block.
+
+- Make the pet icon/identity the visual anchor.
+- Use a three-row hierarchy: identity, observed total XP, observed rate.
+- Add a small “observed” badge instead of repeating caveats in every line.
+- Use a stable panel width and truncate long pet names with an ellipsis.
+
+### Yandex Music
+
+Current custom panel is the right direction, but it needs the same surface contract as Move Hotbar.
+
+- Use a 52 px cover tile with rounded clipping and fallback icon.
+- Give service/playing labels a consistent eyebrow hierarchy.
+- Use a stable title/artist column so long metadata cannot resize the card.
+- Keep progress rail at a fixed y position.
+- Reserve a two-line lyric region with clipping and animated line transitions.
+- Use a cover-loading shimmer while the image is in flight.
+- Show explicit connection state in the settings panel: local, account, waiting, backoff, error.
+
+### Waypoint Route, Map Info, Simon Says
+
+These are high-information dungeon overlays and need density control.
+
+- Use compact cards with a single accent family per solver.
+- Separate primary result from secondary context using opacity, not extra borders.
+- Keep route progress and room/secret counts in fixed-width slots.
+- Use a consistent “active / waiting / unavailable” indicator.
+
+### Inventory HUD, Item Name HUD, Skill Progress HUD, Scoreboard
+
+These display frequently changing values and are vulnerable to jitter and overflow.
+
+- Calculate content width before rendering.
+- Clamp and ellipsize names.
+- Align values on a baseline grid.
+- Use one shared card background and one shared divider treatment.
+- Use a theme preset rather than one-off colors per feature.
+
+### Stopwatch and DVD Bounce
+
+These are expressive HUDs but should still obey the benchmark.
+
+- Stopwatch: stable-width digits, segmented display option, active glow only while running.
+- DVD: keep motion, but use the selected theme accent and smooth easing at wall collisions; avoid flashing the entire card.
+
+## Visual renderers and world overlays
+
+These are not traditional panels, but they are still GUI/HUD-facing graphics and must share semantic styling:
+
+- Player Glow: reduce outline intensity at distance; use theme accent and avoid opaque silhouettes.
+- Nametags: stable plate width, health bar as a secondary rail, no text collision.
+- Block Outline: preserve world readability; use theme accent only for selected/confirmed state.
+- Titanium ESP: use one scanner color and a distinct confirmed/commission color.
+- Ambient Particles: tie particle color to the theme preset; cap brightness and density.
+- Rotating Item: preserve the visual motion but reuse accent and shadow tokens.
+- Skybox: expose palette presets that coordinate with GUI presets without changing vanilla fog semantics.
+- Held Item Shader: map Smoke/Stars/Portal/Galaxy to the same semantic accent palette.
+- Motion Blur: keep temporal effect separate from UI surfaces; never blur text or controls.
+- No Render, Aspect, Fog, and Ambience: expose clear preview/status text; avoid controls that imply a visual result when the current world does not support it.
+
+## Dedicated screens and nested editors
+
+### Waypoint name screen
+
+- Use a centered modal card with clear title, field focus ring, character counter, and explicit Cancel/Save hierarchy.
+- Reserve an error row below the field instead of shifting the modal when validation changes.
+
+### Key capture screen
+
+- Show device type, current binding, and a large “Press a key” state.
+- Give Escape and Backspace explicit help text.
+- Use the same modal surface and error styling as settings panels.
+
+### Knife browser / asset browser
+
+- Add a thumbnail skeleton state, selected card glow, filter/search grouping, and a persistent download status strip.
+- Keep destructive/reset actions visually separated from browsing actions.
+
+### Config, command binds, command shortcuts, chat commands, leap message, route, puzzle solvers, and visual editors
+
+- Convert long ungrouped lists to section cards.
+- Use stable labels and inline validation rows.
+- Place Add/Create actions in the section header; place Delete/Reset actions at the bottom with warning styling.
+- Preserve current instant-save behavior and never add fake Save buttons.
+
+## Ready-to-use shared surface painter
+
+The following abstraction should replace one-off flat panels over time. It mirrors Move Hotbar’s visual contract while remaining usable by integer-based GUI code:
+
+```kotlin
+object PremiumSurface {
+    enum class Preset { MINIMAL, GLASS, NEON, AMBER }
+
+    data class Style(
+        val preset: Preset,
+        val background: java.awt.Color,
+        val secondary: java.awt.Color,
+        val accent: java.awt.Color,
+        val opacity: Float = .92f,
+        val radius: Float = 6f,
+        val border: Float = 1f,
+        val shadow: Boolean = true,
+        val glow: Boolean = false,
+        val shimmer: Boolean = false,
+        val speed: Float = 1f,
+    )
+
+    fun style(preset: Preset, accent: java.awt.Color): Style = when (preset) {
+        Preset.MINIMAL -> Style(preset, java.awt.Color(22,32,46), java.awt.Color(28,42,58), accent)
+        Preset.GLASS -> Style(preset, java.awt.Color(27,39,55), java.awt.Color(41,58,78), accent, .72f, 7f, 1f, true, false, true, .6f)
+        Preset.NEON -> Style(preset, java.awt.Color(14,24,39), java.awt.Color(23,42,66), accent, .94f, 6f, 1.25f, true, true, true, 1f)
+        Preset.AMBER -> Style(preset, java.awt.Color(31,27,24), java.awt.Color(55,42,31), java.awt.Color(255,184,77), .92f, 6f)
+    }
+}
+```
+
+## Implementation order
+
+1. Centralize `PremiumSurface` and route `ChromeDraw` and `GuiKit.section` through it.
+2. Upgrade `NoFrillsClickGui`, `SettingsPanel`, and `HudEditorScreen` because every feature inherits their visual quality.
+3. Migrate high-frequency HUDs: Player Display, timers, Inventory, Skill, Item Name, Scoreboard, Yandex Music.
+4. Migrate dungeon cards and world-overlay accents.
+5. Add per-feature preset selection only where a feature has enough visual area to benefit; do not add hypothetical settings everywhere.
+6. Render and visually inspect at 960x540, 1280x720, and 1920x1080 in Minecraft. The Linux build environment cannot certify this step.
+
+## Acceptance checklist
+
+- No HUD overlaps or clips at the three target resolutions.
+- No text changes the panel width while values update.
+- Every interactive control has a visible hover/focus/pressed state.
+- Errors and unavailable states are readable without relying on color alone.
+- Glow/shimmer never reduces text contrast.
+- Glass presets use alpha and sheen, not claims of world blur.
+- Reduced-motion preference is respected where the platform exposes it.
+- HUD editor bounds match live renderer bounds.
+- Feature panels remain usable with keyboard navigation and scroll.
+- The final result is visually inspected in-game; compilation alone is not a design sign-off.
